Package: inkr
Title: CSS-Like Styling Language for Terminal User Interfaces
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person(given = "TODO-GIVEN-NAME", family = "TODO-FAMILY-NAME",
           email = "todo-maintainer@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Ink for R is a CSS-like styling language and engine for
    terminal user interfaces. It parses stylesheets written in the 'inkr'
    language (files with the '.inkr' extension), compiles them into typed
    declarations, matches selectors against a logical element tree, applies
    the cascade and inheritance to produce computed styles, and explains how
    a value was obtained. A computed style can then be adapted to terminal
    colors, text attributes and border characters for an explicitly given set
    of terminal capabilities, and serialized as ANSI escape sequences. The
    package does not render widgets or lay out a terminal, and has no
    dependency on any terminal user interface framework.
